1500:
(a) Due date of taxes. The tax imposed by this article shall become due and payable from the occupant at the time of occupancy of any hotel in this county. All amounts of such taxes collected by an operator are due and payable to the business license office between the first and 20th day of the calendar month next following the calendar month or fiscal period for which the return is being filed.
(b) Filing of monthly return. Each operator or person liable for payment of the tax under this article shall file a return and pay the occupancy tax due monthly with the supervisor in such form as the supervisor may reasonably prescribe.
(c) Contents of return. All returns filed under this article shall show and include:
(1) The gross rent;
(2) Rent from permanent residents;
(3) Rents exempt from tax;
(4) Taxable rent;
(5) Amount of tax collected or otherwise due for the related period;
(6) Such other information as is required by the supervisor; and
(7) Payment of the tax due including any penalties and interest.
(d) Delivery of return and remittance. The operator, who is required by this section to file the return, shall deliver the return, together with the remittance in full of the full amount of tax due and all penalties, interests, and delinquent taxes due to the business license office by the twentieth of the month following the month the tax was collected.
(e) Collection fee allowed operators. Operators collecting the tax shall be allowed a percentage of the tax due and accounted for and shall be reimbursed in the form of a deduction in submitting, reporting and paying the amount due, if such amount is not delinquent at the time of payment. The rate of the deduction shall be three percent of the amount due, but only if the amount due was not delinquent at the time of payment.
(f) Extension of time for filing return and paying tax. For good cause, the supervisor may extend, for a period not to exceed one month, the time for making any return or payment of tax. No further extension of time may be granted. Any person to whom an extension of time has been granted who makes a return and pays the tax within the period of extension shall pay, in addition to the tax, interest on the amount thereof at the rate of one percent per month, or fraction thereof, for the period of such extension to the time of return and payment.
(Res. of 2-8-77, § 8; Ord. of 10-24-89, § III; Code 1977, § 3-15.1-8; Ord. of 7-10-01)
State Law reference— Dealer's commission, O.C.G.A. § 48-13-52.

